author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Writing a hierarchy dependency row is validated against the declared hierarchyDirection of its kind, and a row whose direction contradicts an existing scalar parent, or which would give a node more incoming child rows than the declared cardinality permits, is refused with a structured error naming both endpoints; Every hierarchy dependency kind resolves into the same internal parent relation that the scalar parent field feeds, so pm list --parent, pm get --tree, and the graph traversals return one answer regardless of which channel recorded the edge; pm validate reports a divergence between the dependency-row hierarchy and the scalar parent hierarchy as a data-quality warning class with the offending ids named, and the class starts at the seven known inverted rows so the count can only shrink; pm graph audit gains a direction-violation finding and a cardinality-violation finding at a severity above info, proven by a negative-control fixture that writes one inverted row and one over-cardinality row; A remediation path exists that retires a single misdirected row without deleting every row sharing its id and kind pair, closing the gap pm-flnefm records; The declared registry becomes the single source: a test asserts that every accepted hierarchy spelling has a declared direction and cardinality and that no code path canonicalizes a hierarchy kind by a rule not stated in the registry"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Made the relationship-kind registry authoritative for hierarchy direction and cardinality across writes and reads, with structured findings and provenance-exact single-row repair."
expected_result: "Child and parent relationship spellings resolve to their declared hierarchy endpoints, enforce cardinality, agree with scalar parents, and support exact safe remediation."
actual_result: "Child rows could be inverted or over-cardinal without validation and were invisible to scalar-only readers; the completed implementation now normalizes, rejects, reports, and repairs those cases."
